[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m## `PacedTerminalWriter` paces across turns — 2026-11-20[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m`996a7b4` makes the budget per frame. Time spent inside `Terminal.write` is[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46msummed across `write()` calls, and once `frameBudget` (8 ms) of it has been[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mspent since the last frame, further chunks are queued until a frame has been[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mproduced. The check is made before a chunk is written, never after: with a PTY[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mthe chunk that has to wait arrives on a later turn. A chunk arriving after a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mframe interval (17 ms) with no write starts a fresh budget and is written at[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46monce — the frame is inferred from the idleness — so ordinary interactive output[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mis not delayed. If the frame waited for has not come within 100 ms, the writer[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mstops waiting for it and, until it comes, leaves one frame interval between[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mbudgets, so a window whose frames have stopped keeps draining and replies the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mterminal owes still go out. Public API unchanged.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mAcceptance, one interleaved run, MiB/s / frames / longest gap ms:[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m| config | ascii | unicode | cjk |[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m|---|---|---|---|[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m| unpaced | 72.1 / 8 / 206 | 26.4 / 2 / 1825 | 22.3 / 1 / 2747 |[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m| writer before `996a7b4` | 67.9 / 6 / 318 | 25.6 / 1 / 2321 | 21.4 / 2 / 2847 |[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m| writer after | 53.6 / **100 / 19** | 22.9 / **245 / 48** | 19.4 / **322 / 23** |[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m| `paced-span`, for reference | 55.4 / 93 / 22 | 23.0 / 240 / 51 | 19.7 / 316 / 22 |[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mThe writer now lands on the bench-only pacer: throughput within 4%, frames and[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mgaps alike. Against unpaced in the same run it costs 13-26% of throughput and[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mtakes the longest gap from 0.2-2.7 s to 19-48 ms. The binary measured here[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mdiffered from what shipped only in the no-frame fallback below, which a 48 ms[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mgap does not reach; a second run of the shipped code gave 54.6 / 97 / 24,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m22.9 / 245 / 50 and 19.5 / 322 / 23.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m**Measured, rejected:** when no frame comes, yielding one event-loop turn[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mbetween budgets instead of a frame interval. Measured with a `waitForFrame`[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mthat never completes while the window stays visible (`XB_PACED=3`): 57.0 /[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m26.0 / 21.8 MiB/s, but longest gaps of 260 / 1039 / 1364 ms — back-to-back[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mbudgets starve the frames as unpaced output does. With the frame interval that[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mshipped, the same setup gives gaps of 102 / 51 / 33 ms at 25.4 / 9.6 / 7.3[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mMiB/s, about a third of unpaced. So a window whose frames have stopped, or[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mwhose frames the writer does not hear about, drains at about a third of the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mnormal rate. A truly hidden window was not measured.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mWhat this does not cover. Tests 1104, all passing. With a visible window the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m100 ms timeout has not been seen to matter: the longest gap in any round of the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mfixed writer was 63 ms on ascii, unicode and cjk and 87 ms on `sgr` (next[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46msection), on one machine. Whether it fired was not counted. There is still no back pressure in the class: the queue takes[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46meverything the PTY delivers, up to 59034 chunks here, about 57 MiB at 0.99 KiB[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46ma chunk (derived). How long input takes to show its effect — a Ctrl-C's output[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mbehind that queue — was not measured. And the class stays opt-in: nothing in[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mthe package uses it.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m```sh[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m# paced-old: a build at ba46f04, recipe as under *In the app*, into /tmp/app-old[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mAPP_OLD=/tmp/app-old/example.app/Contents/MacOS/example \[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  script/term_compare/spike.sh /tmp/pay /tmp/accept 5 "unpaced paced-old paced paced-span paced-noframe"[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mpython3 script/term_compare/spike_table.py /tmp/accept[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m```[m
