[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m## Grapheme-join fast paths — 2026-11-19[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m`Buffer._joinsPreviousGrapheme` decides whether a code point continues the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mcluster in the cell before it. Whatever its exits do not settle goes to[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m`characters` segmentation, which allocates. Each change below adds or widens an[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mexit that is decided by the incoming code point, its width and the last code[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mpoint the previous cell stores, and each holds because of one rule of UAX #29:[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **The known cell width is passed in.** `writeChar` has already looked up[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  `wcwidth(codePoint)`; the check looked it up again, which above the BMP is a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  binary search.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **A wide code point joins only after Prepend, a leading jamo or ZWJ.** No[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  wide code point is Extend (bar the emoji modifiers, which have their own[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  check), Hangul V or T, a regional indicator or an Indic consonant, so only[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  GB9b, GB6 and GB11 can attach one to the cluster before it, and each is[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  decided by the last code point stored. Replaces the wide-after-wide exit,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  Hangul exclusion and both `wcwidth` calls.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **A zero-width Extend or ZWJ always joins, unless the cell ends in a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  control.** GB9 attaches them to anything; GB4 is the exception, and a cell[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  can end in a control — U+2028 is width 1, and with mode 2027 off any[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  zero-width code point is stored. `zeroWidthExtends` takes whole stretches,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  Greek to Mongolian, minus Prepend, controls, Hangul V and T, and the marks[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  the width table knows from a newer Unicode than the segmenter.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **A narrow letter joins only by GB9b or GB9c.** `isNarrowLetter` — Hebrew to[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  NKo, Thai, Lao, Georgian, the Latin and Greek extended blocks, and the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  independent vowels and consonants of the ten Indic blocks — is no Extend,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  jamo, regional indicator or pictograph, so it starts a new cluster unless the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  cell ends in Prepend or holds a conjunct linker. It runs after the Indic[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  conjunct check, which can join pairs GB9c does not.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **Indic vowel signs join.** At width 1, the dependent vowel signs at offsets[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  0x3E-0x4C of Devanagari to Malayalam are SpacingMark or Extend (GB9a, GB9),[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  bar the unassigned code points between them.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **A valid emoji modifier joins.** Past the modifier-base check a modifier is[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  Extend, so GB9 applies.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **The line is read once.** `currentLine` goes through the circular buffer on[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  every call, and the check called it up to three times; `_previousCellIndex` is[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  inlined into the same read.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m- **Plane 1 gets a width table.** `wcwidth` binary-searched everything above[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  the BMP. Plane 1, where nearly every emoji lives, now has a 64 KiB table like[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  the BMP's, filled in `wcwidth`'s own precedence, combining over wide.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
