[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m## [6.5.0] - 2026-11-16[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mThis release comes out of a review of the package for speed and resource use.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mEvery number below was measured before and after, ten interleaved rounds of[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mthe old build against the new on an idle Apple M1 Pro, AOT-compiled, 170x50[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mgrid with 10000 lines of scrollback; medians, with the two builds' ranges[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mdisjoint in every row.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m### Faster[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Output whose lines end in `ESC[K` - what `grep --color` and compiler[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  diagnostics emit on every line - no longer grows each line's storage to the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  full width of the window. Erasing allocated and wrote cells that already[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  read as blank, which undid the line storage 6.3.0 sized from the text, for[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  exactly the output that is kept in scrollback. Lines ending in `ESC[K` write[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  at 130 MiB/s instead of 63.5, `grep --color`-shaped output at 39 instead of[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  12, and 10000 such lines hold 14.6 MB of cell storage instead of 29.3[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  (9.8 MB for 30-column lines).[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Box drawing, block elements, braille and the dash, quote and bullet[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  punctuation (U+2010..U+2027) are written in batched runs. They took the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  per-character path with a full grapheme segmentation each, so a TUI's[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  borders and bars were written at 4.6 M characters/s; they now go at 125.5.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  Turkish text with an em dash on each line goes from 82 to 136 MiB/s.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* OSC 8 hyperlinks no longer rescan the whole buffer as they are written.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  With a link on every line (`ls --hyperlink`) and 10000 lines of scrollback,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  writing took 1.8 ms a line; it takes 4.3 us. At 1000 lines, 7.2 us becomes[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  3.9 us, and plain output scrolling past a single live link is 17% faster.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* The paragraph cache is sized to the screen. Its keys carry each cell's[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  colour, and at a fixed 2048 entries a screen with a colour per cell - a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  truecolor gradient, 256-colour output - missed on nearly every cell of[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  every repaint, cursor blink included. It now holds one screen plus a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  quarter, and never less than before.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mPlain ASCII, long lines, SGR-heavy output, Cyrillic and alt-screen redraws are[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46munchanged. CJK text measured about 2% slower (9.3 to 9.1 M characters/s).[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m### Changed behaviour[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* With the OSC 8 registry at its 4096-link ceiling, it is re-checked for[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  links that are no longer on screen once per interval rather than on every[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  new link. A link opened while the registry is full still gets no link, as[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  before; links freed by an erase are picked up within at most 2048 opens[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  instead of at the next one.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* The paragraph cache can hold more than 2048 entries per view: about 10800[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  at 170x50. Only a screen that needs that many distinct entries reaches it.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m### API[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `BufferLine.writtenLength`: the cells from here to `length` hold nothing.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `TerminalPainter.fitParagraphCacheToGrid`, and `ParagraphCache.maximumSize`[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  is now settable.[m
