    perf(ui): size the paragraph cache to the grid it has to hold
    
    Paragraph cache keys carry the cell's colour, so a screen where most
    cells differ in colour - a truecolor gradient, 256-colour output - needs
    about one entry per cell. The cache held 2048 whatever the grid, and a
    cache smaller than one screen does not degrade, it stops working: cells
    are looked up in the same order every frame, so each frame evicts what
    the next one needs. At 130x62, 8060 lookups per repaint missed 8046 to
    8060 times, cursor blink included. This is the fault the procedural
    glyph cache had at 512 entries.
    
    The cache is now sized each paint to the cells on screen plus a quarter,
    so the eviction batch cannot cut into a full screen, and never below the
    configured size. `ParagraphCache.maximumSize` is mutable for that.
    
    Measured as hit rate, in a widget test that fails without the change: a
    screen with a colour per cell goes from 0% to one miss per frame, the
    cell that changed. Frame time in profile mode and the memory held by a
    full cache were not measured. The ceiling per view rises from 2048
    entries to about 10800 at 170x50, reached only by content that needs it.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

