[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  twice (rows, then columns).[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `TerminalView` no longer answers OSC 52 clipboard reads by default. It[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  installed its own query handler, so any remote output could read the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  user's clipboard while the view had focus. An embedder that wants this[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  sets `Terminal.onClipboardQuery` itself. Clipboard writes are unchanged.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* The window title report (`CSI 21 t`) always returns an empty title. It[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  echoed the application-set title into the input stream, which let output[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  place text on the shell's command line.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `TerminalView(readOnly: true)` blocks hardware keyboard input and paste,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  as documented. Only the soft keyboard was blocked before. Copy and[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  select-all still work. On web, `readOnly` still opens an input[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  connection, so typed text can reach the terminal there.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m### Escape parser and terminal[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* CSI numeric parameters are capped at 65535. Larger values overflowed,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  threw a `RangeError` out of `write()` and dropped the rest of the chunk[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  (`CSI 18446744073709551615 L`); a huge REP count stalled the terminal.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  REP also repeats at most one screenful.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Malformed OSC 133 `cmdline_url`, XTGETTCAP and OSC colour values no[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  longer throw from `write()` or produce negative colours. DECAUPSS ignores[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  malformed designators, so DECRQUPSS cannot echo control characters.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Unrecognised ESC sequences with intermediate bytes (`ESC % G`,[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  `ESC SP F`, `ESC $ ( D`) are discarded instead of printing their final[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  character.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Colon-form truecolor SGR without a colour-space field (`38:2:R:G:B`) is[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  parsed correctly when more parameters follow.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* An OSC whose terminator arrives exactly at the 8 KiB limit no longer[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  swallows the terminator and all following output.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* RIS (`ESC c`) clears OSC colour overrides, DECAC colour assignments and[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  saved DEC private modes.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* In origin mode with left/right margins, VPA no longer drifts the cursor[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  to the right, and CHA/HPA are relative to the left margin.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Pasting text with CRLF line endings outside bracketed paste mode sends[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  one carriage return per line, not two.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Search and URL detection no longer see a phantom space where a wide[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  character wrapped to the next row.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* XTVERSION and secondary device attributes report the current package[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  version; they had been reporting 5.3.0.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m### Buffer, reflow and selection[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* The cursor stays in place when a resize makes a line exactly fill the new[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  width. It was left on its old row, and the next character overwrote the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  last one. A narrowing reflow also no longer pushes the cursor's row into[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  scrollback while blank rows remain below it.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `ESC[K` no longer breaks soft-wrapped lines unless it erases the whole[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  row. `grep --color` and compiler diagnostics emit it constantly, which[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  split long lines when they were copied or reflowed.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Erased or reflowed text no longer reappears after shrinking and then[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  widening the terminal.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Copied text keeps the spaces between words when an application left the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  cells blank instead of writing spaces, as ncurses does.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  `BufferLine.getText()` and `toString()` now return a space for a blank[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  cell inside the row; trailing blanks are still trimmed.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Lines scrolled out of a scroll region that starts at the top of the main[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  screen are kept in scrollback, so output above a pinned status line (the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  apt/dpkg progress bar layout) is no longer lost.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Block selections dragged from top-right to bottom-left are highlighted.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Restoring a saved cursor after the terminal height shrinks and grows[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  returns to the right row.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m### View and input[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Mouse reports are no longer one row too low once there is scrollback and[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  the view height is not a multiple of the cell height. With the view[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  scrolled up, a click reports the screen row of the line actually clicked[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  instead of the visible row index.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Scrolling back to the bottom while output is streaming resumes following[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  new output.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* With a full scrollback, a scrolled-up view keeps the same text in place[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  as new output arrives, until that text is trimmed.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `TerminalTheme` has value equality, so rebuilding an equal non-const[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  theme no longer flushes the render caches or sends an unsolicited[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  colour-scheme report.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* With xterm modifyOtherKeys level 2, unmodified and Shift-only printable[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  keys are sent as plain text again instead of `CSI 27 ; 1 ; … ~`, and Meta[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  is encoded. On macOS this also lets those keys reach the input method.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Cancelling an IME composition no longer sends a backspace that erased a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  real character on the shell line.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Output that only looks like a ZModem start no longer freezes the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  session; the bytes are shown and input keeps working.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
