    fix(input): send modified keypad Enter as Enter under kitty disambiguate
    
    6.3.4 made unmodified keypad Enter a carriage return for clients that push
    only the kitty "disambiguate" flag, but with a modifier held it still went
    out as `CSI 57414;2u`. Cursor's agent CLI does not decode keypad key codes
    and inserted U+E046 where Shift+Enter starts a new line.
    
    Unless every key is reported as an escape code, keypad Enter is now encoded
    exactly as the main Enter key: a carriage return, or `CSI 13;2u` with Shift.
    Checked against cursor-agent 2026.09.28 in a pty: `CSI 13;2u` and
    `CSI 13;130u` (Num Lock set) start a new line, `CSI 57414;2u` and
    `CSI 57414;130u` insert U+E046. With every key an escape code, keypad Enter
    keeps its own code.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

