Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 19:57:00 2026 +0300

    fix(input): send keypad text and Enter as typed under kitty disambiguate
    
    Cursor's agent CLI pushes only the kitty "disambiguate" flag (`CSI >1u`)
    and does not decode the keypad key codes. Every numpad digit or operator
    went out as `CSI 57400;129u` and the like, and the CLI inserted the
    private-use character U+E038 instead of `1`. Num Lock (Clear on a Mac
    keyboard) and keypad Enter did the same.
    
    The spec reports only non-text keypad keys under disambiguate, so the
    digits and operators now follow the same rules as other text keys: plain
    text unless Ctrl, Alt or Super is held or every key is an escape code.
    kitty counts Caps Lock, Num Lock and Scroll Lock as modifiers, so they
    are reported only when every key is an escape code.
    
    Unmodified keypad Enter now sends a carriage return like the main Enter
    key. kitty and Ghostty send `CSI 57414u` there, which leaves the key
    dead in clients that only ask for disambiguate; with a modifier or under
    report-all it is still encoded.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

