    fix(ui): shrink wide glyphs that overflow their cells instead of clipping
    
    A wide character is almost always an emoji, drawn from a color emoji font
    whose advance (about 1.25em for Apple Color Emoji) exceeds two cells of
    most monospace faces. The painter clipped it to its two cells, shaving
    off the right edge of every ✅ and ❌. Scale an overflowing glyph in a
    wide cell down to the cells it owns, vertically centred on where it
    would have been drawn. Narrow cells keep clipping.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
