Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 00:49:55 2026 +0300

    fix(input): type Option-composed characters under modifyOtherKeys
    
    On macOS Option composes characters unless option-as-meta is on: on a
    Turkish Q layout Option+Q is `@`. With xterm's modifyOtherKeys mode 2
    enabled, which Claude Code and other Ink apps turn on to tell
    Shift+Enter apart, that press was encoded as `CSI 27;3;64~`, Alt+`@`.
    The application read a modified key, not a character, and `@` could
    not be typed at all.
    
    The kitty handler already treated such a press as text. The check now
    lives in `composed_text.dart`, shared by both encoders, and
    modifyOtherKeys sends the composed character as typed. Option on a key
    that composes nothing is still Alt, and so is Option with Ctrl or Cmd;
    other platforms are unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
