    fix(selection): start a selection on blank space too
    
    `selectWord` returned without setting anything when the cell under the
    pointer was a separator or one of the empty cells that make up most of a
    sparse screen. It is the entry point for touch selection — long press,
    long-press drag, and the first event of a non-mouse drag — as well as for
    double click, so a press that landed on blank space selected nothing and
    could not recover: every later move update re-read the same blank
    starting cell and returned again.
    
    A cell that is part of no word now selects itself, which is what the drag
    needs something to grow from. The same fallback applies to the far end of
    the range, where bailing out had frozen an extending selection at
    whatever it covered when the pointer crossed a space.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

