Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Thu Sep 17 20:07:09 2026 +0300

    fix(buffer): keep scrolled lines attached to the buffer
    
    The three full-width scroll paths shifted a block of lines by assigning
    `lines[to] = lines[from]`, which leaves the same `BufferLine` in both
    slots of the circular buffer. Overwriting the stale slot later ran
    `_adoptChild`, whose first act is to detach whatever the slot holds — by
    then a line living at `to`, on screen, and carrying anchors.
    
    A detached line cannot answer for an anchor, so `TerminalController`
    reported no selection at all: nothing highlighted, nothing to copy. Each
    scrolled line took another line down with it, so a session degraded the
    longer it ran — after browsing a log in `vi` at 59 rows, 40 of the 59
    lines on screen could no longer be selected.
    
    Only the alternate screen was affected. The main buffer scrolls by
    pushing new lines onto the scrollback and never reaches this code, which
    is why the same file was selectable straight out of `cat` and not out of
    an editor.
    
    `IndexAwareCircularBuffer.move` does the shift with the source slot
    cleared, so no element is ever reachable from two slots. All three call
    sites refill the slots they vacate, which they already did.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

