    ci: keep the cross-package harness out of `flutter analyze`
    
    `flutter analyze` at the repository root resolves the root package and
    `example/` - it runs `pub get` for the latter itself - but not an arbitrary
    nested package, so `script/cross_bench/` was analyzed inside the root context
    where `package:xterm` and `package:xterm2` do not exist. Two `uri_does_not_exist`
    errors, and CI runs with `--fatal-infos`.
    
    Excluded rather than resolved. Making CI `pub get` the harness would put two
    pub.dev packages on the critical path of every run, so an unrelated retraction
    or resolution failure would turn this package's CI red; the harness is verified
    by being run, which is the only way its numbers mean anything anyway.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
