    Two phases off the write-path front.
    
    Phase 5.5 closes CSI parameter bulk scanning for the third and last
    time, and closes it on arithmetic rather than on another benchmark: a
    bulk scanner pays setup once per parameter and earns it back once per
    digit past the first, so on altscreen it makes 300 calls to remove 191.
    script/csi_param_census.dart counts that. The implementation is not
    merged; the counter and the record are.
    
    Phase 6.1 stops sizing a line's cell store to the viewport. A line is
    born holding a shared empty list, so scrolling allocates nothing per
    line, and the first write sizes the store to what it writes. parse_bench
    over five interleaved rounds: ascii +18%, cyrillic +19%, utf8 +24%,
    altscreen flat, ascii-long-lines -3%, sgr -13%. Retained scrollback at
    10000 lines drops 2.0x for 90-column output and 3.0x for 60-column
    output, unchanged for full-width.
    
    sgr is a real regression and is documented as one in RENDER_PLAN.md
    phase 6.1: the line is filled by six short runs, so it takes two
    allocations where one would do, and no growth policy gets it to one.
    
