[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  the front, enough stale entries pushed a still-valid prompt out — the[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  terminal forgot a prompt that was on screen.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Escape-heavy output parses faster. `ByteConsumer.consume()` ran the same[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  high-surrogate test twice per code point to reach the same conclusion, that a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  unit which does not start a surrogate pair is one unit long and is its own[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  code point. Testing once covers everything outside astral text. The gain[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  lands where `consume()` is hot: SGR-heavy output goes from 76 to 81 MiB/s end[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  to end and 121 to 133 MiB/s through the parser, alt-screen output from 171 to[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  178 and 276 to 296. Plain text is unchanged, since it goes through the run[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  scan instead.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* `wholeWord` search no longer builds a one-character `String` and runs a[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  Unicode regex per side of every candidate match. An ASCII range check up[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  front takes the overhead from 10% to 1-3%, and 14.3 ms to 12.9 ms on output[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  where matches abut word characters.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m* Plain-text URL detection runs only while the hyperlink modifier is held. It[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46m  used to run on every pointer hover — 1.3 to 1.9 us and about 3 KB per event —[m
