Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Sat Aug 29 10:09:38 2026 +0300

    fix: act on the review findings that survived checking
    
    A code review raised thirteen items. Nine checked out against the code and
    are addressed here; `bin/review_bench.dart` measures the ones that can be
    measured, and BENCHMARKS.md records the results including the two that
    turned out neutral.
    
    Correctness:
    
    - `_pruneSemanticPromptAnchors` only dropped stale anchors from the front,
      so anchors invalidated in the middle stayed. The queue is capped at the
      buffer's line count and that cap evicts from the front, so enough stale
      entries push a still-valid prompt out and the terminal forgets a prompt
      that is on screen. Now a full sweep, and the three callers stop
      re-validating since nothing stale survives it. Regression test included;
      it fails against the old prune.
    - `CursorStyle.isItalis` is spelled `isItalic`, with a deprecated alias, and
      `isStrikethrough` fills the gap next to it. Both are public API through
      `lib/core.dart`.
    
    Measured wins:
    
    - `wholeWord` search took a one-character `String` and a Unicode regex per
      side of every candidate match. An ASCII range check up front takes the
      overhead from 10% to 1-3%, and 14.3 ms to 12.9 ms where matches abut word
      characters.
    - Plain-text URL detection ran on every pointer hover whether or not the
      hyperlink modifier was down, at 1.3-1.9 us and about 3 KB per event, for a
      result nothing could act on. It now runs only while the modifier is down,
      and once more when the modifier goes down under a stationary pointer so a
      link still lights up without moving the mouse.
    - `_notifyEditableRect` walked to the root on every terminal change. Fifty
      writes between frames were fifty `localToGlobal` walks to publish a rect
      observable once; it is now marked dirty and flushed from `paint`. A test
      pins 50 writes to one report.
    - Key handling counted runes to ask whether a string was one code point.
      `singleCodePoint` answers in 3 ns instead of 25.
    
    Measured neutral, kept anyway:
    
    - `BufferLine.hasAnchors` keeps reflow from building an `UnmodifiableListView`
      per line, including inside its copy loop where it was building one per
      chunk. No timing change.
    - `_oscTail` replaces `_osc.sublist(n).join(';')`, which allocated a list to
      copy strings that usually did not need copying. No timing change, including
      on an 8 KiB OSC 52 payload.
    
    Both remove provably dead work and `hasAnchors` is the API the code wanted;
    neither is claimed as a speedup.
    
    Left alone: `_csi.params` as a fixed `Int32List`, because Phase 5.4 measured
    that loop and found reordering worth nothing and batching worth -8%; and
    `PacedTerminalWriter`'s unbounded queue, which needs a decision about
    dropping output or a threshold API rather than a cleanup commit. That one is
    Phase 7.
    
    Four review items did not survive checking and are not acted on: the
    hyperlink eviction scan is already batched and documented with a test, the
    padding claim mistakes an ancestor `Container` for a coordinate skew, the
    trackpad fling loop is required for per-notch mouse reporting, and the
    controller dispose concern is one redundant notification rather than a crash.
    
