Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Sat Aug 29 01:50:58 2026 +0300

    docs: reject CSI parameter bulk scanning
    
    The candidate the write-path briefing opened with. Two implementations, both
    slower than what they replace, and a free preliminary that measured nothing.
    
    The preliminary first: the digit case sat seventh in `_consumeCsi`'s branch
    chain and digits are about two thirds of the parameter bytes, and none of the
    six tests ahead of it can match 0x30-0x39, so hoisting it is semantically
    identical. It moved `sgr` parser 133 → 132 and `altscreen` 297 → 299, both
    inside the noise. A CSI byte does not pay for the branch chain.
    
    | | sgr full | sgr parser | altscreen full | altscreen parser |
    |---|---|---|---|---|
    | baseline | 81 | 132 | 179 | 298 |
    | run scanner + bulk advance | 74 | 115 | 166 | 267 |
    | scan and accumulate fused | 77 | 121 | 170 | 278 |
    
    The first version read every digit twice and normalised the queue four times
    per run. Fusing the scan into the accumulate loop recovered half the loss and
    still landed 8% down, with the conditions disjoint over three interleaved
    rounds.
    
    The reason ties this to the fast path merged earlier today: `consume()` is now
    one normalisation compare, one block read, one `codeUnitAt` and four field
    updates, and the bulk path replaces `run` of those with an emptiness check,
    two getters that normalise again, a limit computation, a scan loop and a
    `consumeAsciiCodeUnits` that normalises a third time. An `sgr` sequence
    averages 9.6 bytes with one-to-three-digit parameters, so with the first digit
    already consumed there are about 1.5 digits left to amortise that over.
    Phase 5.2 had already closed the gap this was aiming at.
    
    The fuzzer earned its place: the fused version initially called `currentBlock`
    unguarded, which throws when the digit just consumed was the chunk's last byte,
    and `parser_fuzz_test.dart` caught it on three seeds.
    
    That closes all three candidates Phase 5.1 ranked - one merged, two rejected
    with measurements. What is left on the write path is the double `_queue.first`
    access inside `consume()`, and then Phase 6.
    
