    docs: record the consume() fast path measurement
    
    Interleaved A/B, three rounds each, and the baseline table every later
    change starts from. Also notes the discarded first attempt: run back to
    back rather than interleaved, it moved columns that never touch `consume()`
    by 4-8%, which is thermal drift and not a result.
    
    The fast path was Phase 5.1's prescreen for CSI bulk scanning, and it
    answered in that candidate's favour - `consume()` was carrying real cost -
    while narrowing its ceiling from ~19 to ~17 ns per character. The easy part
    is now taken. The next visible remainder in `consume()` is its double
    `_queue.first` access, recorded as a separate candidate because caching the
    active block needs invalidation on `add`, `rollback`,
    `unrefConsumedBlocks` and `reset`.
    
