Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Sun Aug 9 10:37:36 2026 +0300

    feat: separate self-initiated replies from user input
    
    A terminal answers the program on the same wire the user types on: device
    attributes, status and cursor-position reports, colour and size queries,
    terminfo capabilities, focus reports, OSC 52 clipboard reads. Nothing
    downstream can tell the two apart afterwards — an arrow key and a
    cursor-position report are both an escape sequence — but an embedder often
    must. One that reads traffic on onOutput as "the user is typing" gets fooled
    the instant a full-screen program probes the terminal at startup, and one that
    mirrors a session across two terminals answers every query twice.
    
    Terminal.onReply receives those self-initiated replies. It falls back to
    onOutput when unset, so existing callers see no change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

