    right edge it redundantly re-erased a cell the main loop already covers
    instead of the placeholder just past the range, leaving it as an orphan
    still carrying the erased lead's style. Both boundary pre-steps also
    fired for an empty range (start == end), erasing a cell whose pair was
    never touched by the (empty) main loop and tearing apart an otherwise
    intact wide-char pair.
    
    Also fixes the `witdh` parameter typo in setCell/_repairWideCellPairing.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

