    fix(ui): guarantee drain progress in PacedTerminalWriter and de-flake its tests
    
    _drain() checked the frame budget before writing, so a pass could write
    zero chunks and stall; switched to do-while so every pass writes at
    least one chunk before the budget is checked. write() also started the
    first drain pass inline, so a burst of synchronous write() calls could
    never batch - each call's solo drain would finish and return before the
    next call had a chance to enqueue. Deferring the first drain via
    scheduleMicrotask lets the whole burst land in the queue first.
    
    Tests depended on a real 1us Stopwatch budget racing clock resolution,
    which is what made "dispose drops pending output" flaky on master;
    replaced with an injectable, deterministic clock.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

