    Merge perf work: benchmark harness, glyph cache fix, write path
    
    Seven commits measured against 8d938de, the published SoFluffyOS/xterm2 master.
    
    Tooling first, because the existing numbers could not answer the question:
    script/bench-compare.sh A/B-benchmarks two builds on a pinned cell grid, and
    bin/parse_bench.dart measures the write path with no Flutter, separating the
    parser from the buffer writes it drives.
    
    What they found:
    
    - The procedural glyph cache was slower than no cache at a full-screen grid.
      512 entries thrashed at 8500 cells, and a miss costs more than not caching.
      Block elements should never have been cached at all.
    - Latin text ran through the grapheme segmenter after the first accented
      letter, and alphabets that are entirely non-ASCII never used the parser's
      batched write path. Cyrillic 6 -> 84 MiB/s, Turkish 16 -> 57.
    - Line storage reserved 256 cells for a 170-column line.
    
    Also adds PacedTerminalWriter, opt-in, for applications that would rather have
    75 frames per second during a burst than drain it 50% sooner.
    
