    perf(buffer): stop over-allocating line storage
    
    `_calcCapacity` doubled from 64, so a 170-column line reserved 256 cells and
    addressed 170 of them. Scrolling allocates one line per line of output, which
    makes this slack a charge on the hottest path in the terminal rather than a
    one-off.
    
    Rounding up to a multiple of 32 keeps enough headroom to absorb the small
    widenings a resize does, without reserving half a line that is never touched.
    `bin/parse_bench.dart`: `ascii` 92 -> 103 MiB/s, `ascii-long-lines` 129 -> 149,
    `cyrillic` 73 -> 85. `altscreen`, which never allocates a line, is unmoved at
    171, which is the control this wanted.
    
