Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Thu Aug 6 00:12:08 2026 +0300

    perf(ui): stop the glyph cache from losing to no cache at all
    
    Measured against the published package at a 170x50 grid, `boxdraw` UI p50 was
    4.6ms where the build without the cache was 2.9ms. Two faults, both in
    `perf(render): cache rasterised procedural glyphs`.
    
    Keys are (codepoint, cell size, colour), so a screen drawing box lines in many
    colours reaches thousands of live keys - the `boxdraw` workload alone reaches
    3840. Against a 512-entry cache that thrashes: the hit rate fell from 97.1% at
    3700 cells to 75.0% at 8500, and since a miss pays for the recording and the
    insert on top of the drawing, the cache was 1.9ms per frame slower than not
    caching. Capacity is now 4096. 8192 measured no better.
    
    Block elements are one or two `drawRect` calls, and replaying a recorded
    picture per cell puts a picture boundary in the raster command stream for
    every cell - Skia batches worse across many small pictures than across one
    stream, the same effect that kept the line picture cache unmerged. On
    `fullscreen`, which is entirely U+2588 at a 100% hit rate, the cache cost
    0.4ms of raster per frame and saved nothing on the UI thread. They now bypass
    it, and `fullscreen` is back to parity with the published build on both
    threads.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

