[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mtwo `drawRect` calls. Recording that into a `Picture` and replaying it per cell[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mputs a picture boundary in the raster command stream for every cell, and Skia[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mbatches worse across many small pictures than across one stream — the same[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46meffect that sank phase 3 above. On `fullscreen`, which is entirely `U+2588` at[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46ma 100% hit rate, the cache cost 0.4ms of raster per frame and saved nothing on[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mthe UI thread. They now bypass the cache, and `fullscreen` is back to parity[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mwith the published build on both threads.[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m
[38;2;166;226;46m+[m[38;2;166;226;46mThe general lesson, and it is the second time this file records it: **a cache[m
