Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Aug 5 21:09:19 2026 +0300

    refactor(ui): split terminal painting into four passes
    
    _paint was one 185-line body mixing decisions with drawing. It is now
    _paintSurface plus four named passes: static backgrounds, overlay backgrounds,
    static foregrounds, overlay foregrounds. Drawing order and drawing commands are
    unchanged; the golden tests cover that.
    
    The static passes are deliberately not adjacent. Selection, search highlights
    and the block cursor rectangle have to land on top of the line backgrounds and
    underneath the glyphs, so the two buffer-dependent passes cannot be merged into
    one - anything that later wants to cache a line has to record its background
    and its foreground separately, with the overlay pass in between.
    
    Cursor state is resolved once per frame into _CursorPaintState instead of three
    times. Each of _cursorRenderColumn, _cursorRenderWidth and _cursorColors reads
    the cursor cell out of the buffer, and the passes each wanted them. The
    invertsCell getter also replaces four copies of the same
    'block cursor and focused' condition.
    
    Also wires the paint counters from the previous commit into the paint path.
    
    No measurable effect on frame times, which is the expected result for a
    refactor that emits identical draw calls. See BENCHMARKS.md.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

