Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Aug 5 21:09:00 2026 +0300

    perf(ui): make the paint path measurable
    
    Adds TerminalRenderStats, a set of process-wide counters for paints, lines
    visited per paint, and paragraph/glyph cache hit rates, and reports them from
    the benchmark alongside the frame timings. The counters are plain integer
    increments on paths that already do map lookups or paragraph layout.
    
    Adds a 'static' workload to the benchmark: a full screen drawn once, then one
    cell changed per frame. This is the case where the renderer does the most work
    it did not need to do, so it is where any partial-repaint work has to show up.
    The 'idle' scenario originally planned does not exist to be measured - the
    cursor blink timer stops itself after five seconds, so there is no sustained
    idle repaint to sample.
    
    Records the resulting baseline in BENCHMARKS.md. The short version: no workload
    comes close to the 16.7ms frame budget, 'boxdraw' is the most expensive one
    rather than 'fullscreen', and the only measurement that looks wrong is the
    flood test at 48fps, which is the parse-per-write path and not the paint path.
    
