Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Aug 5 20:28:39 2026 +0300

    fix(kitty): follow the protocol's reporting rules for releases and modifiers
    
    Three deviations from the kitty keyboard protocol made a single keystroke
    look like two key events to clients that enable it (observed with omp,
    which pushes flags 5):
    
    - Release events were reported for text-producing keys whenever "report
      event types" was set. The spec reports releases only for keys already
      sent as escape codes, so a plain keystroke arrived as text plus a
      trailing CSI-u that parsers read as a second press.
    - Modifier keys were reported under "disambiguate escape codes" alone.
      The spec reports them only under "report all keys as escape codes".
    - macOS Option-composed characters were encoded as alt+key. On a Turkish
      Q layout Option+Q is how "@" is typed, so the character was lost.
      Composed text now falls through to the text handlers unless the client
      asked for all keys as escape codes.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

