Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Wed Aug 5 20:07:19 2026 +0300

    fix(ui): paint box-drawing bars at their intended weight
    
    Bars were inflated on all four sides by the same `overlap` that closes the
    seam between tiled block elements. For a bar the only seam is the one its
    long axis runs into, so inflating the short axis too made a nominally
    `thin`-wide rule render `thin + 1` px, i.e. roughly double weight at
    terminal font sizes.
    
    Add `fillBar`, which bleeds along the long axis only and snaps the short
    axis to whole logical pixels around the requested centre line - the bars
    paint without antialiasing, so an unsnapped edge otherwise came out one
    pixel wide in one cell and two in the next.
    
    Derive heavy weight from the snapped light stroke instead of an
    independent `width * 0.30`: at a 12px cell the two rounded opposite ways
    and `━` rendered four times `─` instead of twice. Double-line rail spacing
    and arc/diagonal stroke widths follow the same snapped stroke.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

