Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 21:09:58 2026 +0300

    fix(ui): consult symbol fonts before color emoji in the fallback chain
    
    The default fallback listed Apple Color Emoji and its Windows/Linux
    counterparts ahead of every symbol family. Codepoints that default to text
    presentation and are absent from monospace fonts - U+23F8 PAUSE is the one
    that surfaced this, and no monospace family on macOS carries it - therefore
    resolved to the emoji font, dropping a full-color pictograph into a line of
    terminal text where a program had asked for two thin bars.
    
    Moves the symbol families ahead of the emoji ones and adds STIX Two Math,
    which ships with macOS and is the only system family there covering
    Miscellaneous Technical. Emoji codepoints are unaffected: no symbol family
    in the list claims them, so they fall through as before.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

