Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 19:23:10 2026 +0300

    fix(ui): size cells from a reference glyph, not the widest ASCII glyph
    
    _measureCharSize() took the max advance over 0x21..0x7e. On a monospace
    font that is a no-op, but when the resolved family is proportional (an
    app may expose UI fonts such as Inter as a terminal font choice) the cell
    grows to fit '@'/'W' and the grid ends up with far too few columns.
    
    Width now comes from '0', the reference glyph other terminals key off:
    present in near-every font, and given the common advance by any monospace
    face. Height stays a max, sampled over '0'/'M'/'g' so the row still fits
    cap-height and descenders.
    
    Also drop the hardcoded drawBoldTextWithBrightColors in fromTextStyle.
    TextStyle carries no field for it, so the literal only served to defeat
    the constructor default it was duplicating.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

