    Merge verified code-review fixes
    
    Acts on CODE_REVIEW_VERIFIED.md, the verified merge of two AI review reports
    plus an architecture discussion. Only findings that were confirmed against the
    code were acted on; the rest are recorded as rejected claims with evidence.
    
    Bug fixes, all found by the new parser fuzz harness:
    * wide-char lead/placeholder pairing is now enforced inside BufferLine.setCell,
      fixing five separate corruptions that all traced back to the raw storage
      primitive being unaware of the pairing
    * IME composition is deferred until the keyboard commits, so Turkish and CJK
      text no longer reaches the terminal as an uncorrected preview
    * a backspace at offset 0 is recognised as a delete when deleteDetection is off
    
    Performance, each measured rather than assumed:
    * procedural glyphs are rasterised once and cached
    * paragraph cache eviction is O(1) instead of O(n log n)
    * notifyListeners no longer copies the listener list on every write
    * hyperlink URIs are pruned as scrollback is evicted, with the scans batched
    
    Also: an opt-in onUnknownSequence diagnostic callback, a reentrancy assert on
    write(), two API deprecations, tighter BufferLine encapsulation, and a first
    pass at decomposing Terminal.
    
    Testing went from 730 tests that asserted little to 799 that assert invariants,
    plus a seeded fuzz harness green at 50000 rounds. docs/benchmarks records the
    profile-mode measurement that closed out the frame-coalescing and dirty-row
    proposals: no workload exceeds the frame budget, and the worst UI frame during
    a 32 MiB flood is 4.2 ms against 16.7 ms.
    
