Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 23:04:33 2026 +0300

    fix(buffer): enforce wide-char lead/placeholder pairing inside BufferLine.setCell
    
    Went structural instead of a fourth targeted patch. Three previous fixes in
    this family (a39ab68, 8762b25, and the two captured in the prior commit)
    all trace back to the same root problem named in this task: BufferLine's
    raw cell storage knows nothing about the width-2 lead / width-0 placeholder
    pairing convention, so every call site that writes a cell has to remember to
    repair a broken pair itself via clearWideCellAt - and the fuzzer keeps
    finding call sites that forgot, at every threshold increase (5000 rounds
    found one, 20000 found two more, in a call site (Buffer.writeChar's
    "wide char doesn't fit before the margin" filler write) unrelated to any
    previous fix).
    
    Rather than patch that one call site and wait for the fuzzer to find the
    next one, this moves the repair into BufferLine.setCell itself - the single
    primitive every one of these call sites already goes through. Before writing
    a cell, it now checks the two ways a write can break the pairing invariant:
    
      - the target index is currently the width-0 placeholder half of a pair,
        and this write gives it a non-zero width - so its former lead (index-1)
        is erased, since it can no longer claim a valid placeholder;
      - this write is itself a new width-2 lead, and index+1 currently holds an
        unrelated stale wide lead - so that lead (and its own placeholder) is
        erased first, since it would otherwise become an invalid "placeholder"
        for the new pair.
    
    This is intentionally narrow in scope (setCell only - not setContent,
    setWidth, or setCellData, which are lower-level/rarely used and would need
    separate handling for their own idempotency), but it is exactly the
    primitive all 8 in-tree call sites use, including both new bugs found by
    this session's fuzzing run. Erasure uses the CursorStyle already passed to
    setCell, matching the background/erase convention clearWideCellAt already
    uses, so behavior for callers that already did the repair themselves is
    unchanged (erasing an already-empty neighbor is a no-op).
    
    This fixes both regressions captured in the previous commit (seed 0x1337
    round 6200, seed 0xdeadbeef round 6325) without touching any call site.
    XTERM2_FUZZ_ROUNDS=20000 is green; pushed further to 50000 with no new
    failures found in this family (see follow-up report).
    
