    test(fuzz): record two more wide-char/placeholder bugs found at 20000 rounds
    
    Pushing XTERM2_FUZZ_ROUNDS to 20000 turns up two more fuzzer failures in the
    same family as the three already fixed in this branch:
    
      - seed 0x1337, round 6200: line 0 col 42
      - seed 0xdeadbeef, round 6325: line 15 col 87
    
    Both verified against the unmodified baseline (git stash) - pre-existing,
    not regressions from recent fixes - and both share the same invariant
    violation: a width-2 cell followed by a cell that is not a clean
    width-0/code-point-0 placeholder.
    
    Root cause confirmed by instrumenting Buffer.writeChar and re-running both
    seeds: the branch that handles a width-2 character not fitting before the
    right margin (`cellWidth == 2 && _cursorX == rightLimit - 1`) writes a
    width-1/code-point-0 filler cell at `_cursorX` to mark the forced wrap point,
    but - unlike the ordinary write path a few lines below it, which always
    calls `line.clearWideCellAt(_cursorX, ...)` first - never clears `_cursorX`
    first. When cursor positioning (CUP) has left `_cursorX` sitting on the
    placeholder half of an existing wide pair, the filler write corrupts that
    placeholder in place while leaving the neighbouring lead cell still marked
    width 2. The corruption happens well before the round number the fuzz
    harness's periodic (every-25-round) invariant sampler happens to catch it
    at, since the sampler only inspects one random line per check.
    
    Recorded as skip:-ped regressions here, per instructions, before attempting
    any fix, so the knowledge survives even if the fix doesn't land.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

