    fix(buffer): clear stale wide-char leads across the whole exposed range on grow
    
    BufferLine.resize intentionally preserves cell data past the old length
    when growing, so a line can regain its content if it's grown back after
    being shrunk. The existing dangling-lead check (from a39ab68) only
    inspected the single cell at the new boundary, so a wide-char
    lead+placeholder pair frozen mid-pair by an *earlier* resize at a
    *different* boundary could resurface, still broken, somewhere in the
    middle of a later, larger newly-exposed range - reproduced by the fuzzer
    via a resize that regrows a line after several prior shrinks at varying
    widths (seed 0xc0ffee, round 3225 of parser_fuzz_test.dart). Scan the
    entire newly exposed range on every grow instead of just its last
    column, clearing any lead left without a valid placeholder.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

