Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 19:41:01 2026 +0300

    perf(render): cache rasterised procedural glyphs
    
    Box-drawing, Powerline, Braille and legacy-computing symbols are drawn as
    vector paths in procedural_glyphs.dart rather than shaped from a font, so
    every repaint of every cell using one of these rebuilt and rasterised the
    same path again, even on a fully static screen.
    
    Add ProceduralGlyphCache (lib/src/ui/procedural_glyph_cache.dart), an
    LRU cache of ui.Picture keyed on (codePoint, cellSize, color) - the only
    inputs that determine the rasterised result, confirmed by checking every
    use of the incoming Paint inside procedural_glyphs.dart: only
    paint.color is read, everything else (stroke widths, shading alphas) is
    derived purely from cellSize and the codepoint. It follows the same
    min-heap LRU + lazy-repair pattern used by ParagraphCache (see the
    perf(observable) and perf(render): O(1) LRU commits on this branch).
    
    paintProceduralGlyph() gains an optional `cache` parameter (default
    null) so its existing signature and behavior are unchanged for the many
    direct call sites in test/src/ui/procedural_glyphs_test.dart. When a
    cache is supplied, the glyph is recorded once into a Picture at the
    origin (the shape never depends on screen position) and reused by
    translating it into place; when omitted, the original direct-paint path
    runs unchanged.
    
    TerminalPainter now owns a ProceduralGlyphCache instance (default
    capacity 512, configurable via `proceduralGlyphCacheSize`), passes it
    into paintProceduralGlyph at its one call site, clears it at every point
    that already clears the paragraph cache (_clearParagraphCache and the
    devicePixelRatio setter - both cell size and fill colors can change what
    a given key should rasterise to), and disposes it in dispose(). A
    proceduralGlyphCacheLength getter mirrors paragraphCacheLength.
    
    The font-shaping short-circuit at the paintProceduralGlyph call site in
    painter.dart (returns true / skips shaping) is unchanged. Added two
    painter_test.dart cases covering cache reuse across repeated paints of
    the same glyph/color, a fresh entry for a different color, and capacity
    bounding. Full `flutter test`, including the golden image suite, is
    green - no pixel output changed.
    
