    fix(mouse): report pointer motion and drag by default
    
    TerminalController defaulted to {tap, scroll}, so _onPointerMotion
    dropped every hover and drag before it reached the terminal. Applications
    enabling DEC private modes 1002 and 1003 therefore never received mouse
    reports, even though the parser, handlers and SGR encoder all supported
    them: cline's mascot could not follow the pointer, while it works in
    xterm, iTerm2 and Kitty.
    
    Default to PointerInputs.all() instead. Reports stay gated on the mouse
    mode the application requests, so a terminal without mouse reporting
    still emits nothing and text selection is unaffected.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

