Author: klc <m_kilic@outlook.com.tr>
Date:   Sun Aug 2 17:51:41 2026 +0300

    fix(render): snap the cell grid to device pixels
    
    Measured character advances are almost never a whole number of device
    pixels, so `column * cellWidth` landed on a different subpixel phase in
    every column. Aliased fills (procedural block glyphs) then rounded each
    column differently and neighbouring blocks ended up a device pixel apart,
    while glyphs were rasterized at a different phase per cell. Backgrounds
    were drawn antialiased on top of that, leaving a partially covered pixel
    at every cell boundary.
    
    Round the measured cell size to whole device pixels, route every row and
    column origin through a single snapping helper, and drop antialiasing
    from the fills that follow the cell grid.
    
    The painter now needs the device pixel ratio, which the view reads from
    the enclosing MediaQuery.
    
    Rows step in whole device pixels while scrolling instead of sliding, and
    a ligature run whose glyphs would drift off the snapped grid is rejected
    and painted cell by cell.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

