    feat(input): expose resetEditingState for out-of-band input
    
    On-screen key bars send input straight to the terminal, which leaves the
    IME composing against a buffer the terminal has already consumed. Without
    a public reset, embedders reach for SystemChannels.textInput directly and
    push a platform editing state that no longer matches _currentEditingState,
    so the next keystroke arrives with a stale prefix attached.
    
    Expose resetEditingState() on CustomTextEditState and TerminalViewState.
    The public wrapper also clears the composing overlay, which the internal
    callers already do before resetting.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

